  <div class="description-content">
    <div id="notebook-overview" class="content-card">
          <figure class="page-mascot page-mascot--notebook" aria-hidden="true">
            <img src="{{ basePath | default('') }}static/image/any-icon/extension/notebook.png" alt="" width="440" height="482"
              loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          </figure>
      <h2>Notebook</h2>
      <p class="content-intro">
        These notebooks serve as the main entry for our wet-lab documentation of the yeast-based biosensor targeting airborne influenza A virus (IAV). Our PAGER (Protein-fragment Assisted GPCR Expression Reporter) antigen-gated receptor system is built in four independent functional modules. Below you can access experimental records for chassis engineering, humanized G-protein chimera construction, PAGER fusion-receptor assembly, and reporter-module validation respectively. Under each record, the protocols cited in that document are listed by number as they appear in the Protocol page, and each number opens that protocol directly.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div id="notebook-chassis" class="content-card">
      <h2>Chassis Engineering</h2>
      <p class="content-intro">
        This notebook records wet-lab procedures for chassis optimization of our yeast biosensor. We performed CRISPR-Cas9-mediated knockout of endogenous <i>FAR1</i> and <i>SST2</i> in <i>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</i> BY4741, aiming to eliminate cell-cycle arrest and G-protein-signaling negative feedback, so as to improve signal sensitivity for our downstream PAGER antigen-gated receptor system.
      </p>
      <div class="pdf-embed">
        <object class="pdf-embed__object" type="application/pdf"
                data="{{ basePath | default('') }}static/image/lab/wetlab/notebook/notebook-chassis-far1-sst2-knockout.pdf"
                aria-label="Notebook - Construction of the FAR1 SST2 Knockout Yeast Strain">
          <p class="pdf-embed__fallback">This notebook PDF is not available yet.</p>
        </object>
      </div>
      {% set citedProtocols = ["01", "03", "05", "07", "08", "09", "10", "11", "12", "13", "14", "16", "19"] %}
      <div class="notebook-resources">
        <div class="notebook-resources__head">
          <span class="notebook-resources__label">Protocols cited in this record</span>
          <a class="notebook-resources__all" href="{{ basePath | default('') }}wet-lab/protocol.html">All 26 protocols &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <ul class="notebook-protocols">
          {% for id in citedProtocols %}
          <li><a href="{{ basePath | default('') }}wet-lab/protocol.html#protocol-p{{ id }}"><span class="notebook-protocols__no">{{ id }}</span><span class="notebook-protocols__title">{{ protocolTitles[id] | safe }}</span></a></li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div id="notebook-gpa1" class="content-card">
      <h2>Humanized G-Protein Chimera</h2>
      <p class="content-intro">
        This notebook records the humanization engineering of <i>GPA1</i> in <i>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</i> — replacing the native C-terminal KIGII motif with the human Gαq EYNLV sequence to retune G-protein coupling for the PAGER receptor.
      </p>
      <div class="pdf-embed">
        <object class="pdf-embed__object" type="application/pdf"
                data="{{ basePath | default('') }}static/image/lab/wetlab/notebook/notebook-gpa1-humanization.pdf"
                aria-label="Notebook - Humanization Engineering of GPA1 in Saccharomyces cerevisiae">
          <p class="pdf-embed__fallback">This notebook PDF is not available yet.</p>
        </object>
      </div>
      {% set citedProtocols = ["01", "02", "03", "04", "05", "07", "08", "10", "11", "12", "13", "14", "15", "16"] %}
      <div class="notebook-resources">
        <div class="notebook-resources__head">
          <span class="notebook-resources__label">Protocols cited in this record</span>
          <a class="notebook-resources__all" href="{{ basePath | default('') }}wet-lab/protocol.html">All 26 protocols &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <ul class="notebook-protocols">
          {% for id in citedProtocols %}
          <li><a href="{{ basePath | default('') }}wet-lab/protocol.html#protocol-p{{ id }}"><span class="notebook-protocols__no">{{ id }}</span><span class="notebook-protocols__title">{{ protocolTitles[id] | safe }}</span></a></li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div id="notebook-pager" class="content-card">
      <h2>PAGER Fusion Receptor</h2>
      <p class="content-intro">
        This notebook records the construction of the PAGER antigen-gated system for Influenza A virus detection — assembly of the membrane-anchored scFv–Gα–Gγ fusion receptor, yeast transformation, expression validation, and HA-antigen-induced activation detection.
      </p>
      <div class="pdf-embed">
        <object class="pdf-embed__object" type="application/pdf"
                data="{{ basePath | default('') }}static/image/lab/wetlab/notebook/notebook-pager-antigen-gated.pdf"
                aria-label="Notebook - Construction of the PAGER Antigen-Gated System for Influenza A Virus Detection">
          <p class="pdf-embed__fallback">This notebook PDF is not available yet.</p>
        </object>
      </div>
      {% set citedProtocols = ["01", "03", "04", "05", "06", "07", "11", "12", "13", "16", "17", "18", "23"] %}
      <div class="notebook-resources">
        <div class="notebook-resources__head">
          <span class="notebook-resources__label">Protocols cited in this record</span>
          <a class="notebook-resources__all" href="{{ basePath | default('') }}wet-lab/protocol.html">All 26 protocols &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <ul class="notebook-protocols">
          {% for id in citedProtocols %}
          <li><a href="{{ basePath | default('') }}wet-lab/protocol.html#protocol-p{{ id }}"><span class="notebook-protocols__no">{{ id }}</span><span class="notebook-protocols__title">{{ protocolTitles[id] | safe }}</span></a></li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div id="notebook-ste2" class="content-card">
      <h2><i>STE2</i> Gating Engineering</h2>
      <p class="content-intro">
        This notebook records the <i>STE2</i> gating engineering track, in which the native &alpha;-factor receptor was redesigned into an antigen-gated surface receptor: the gating construct (signal peptide&ndash;antagonist&ndash;anti-H1N1_HA nanobody&ndash;ALFA tag&ndash;TEVcs) and its sequence synthesis, amplification of the <i>STE2</i> upstream and downstream homology arms, sgRNA and repair-template assembly, isolation of the gating-engineered strains, the <i>STE2</i>&ndash;yEGFP fusion used for membrane-localisation checks, protein-expression detection, and the functional validation runs.
      </p>
      <div class="pdf-embed">
        <object class="pdf-embed__object" type="application/pdf"
                data="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6373/wiki/lab/wetlab/notebook/notebook-ste2.pdf"
                aria-label="Notebook - STE2 Gating Engineering">
          <p class="pdf-embed__fallback">This notebook PDF is not available yet.</p>
        </object>
      </div>
      {% set citedProtocols = ["01", "03", "04", "05", "07", "08", "09", "10", "11", "12", "13", "14", "18", "20"] %}
      <div class="notebook-resources">
        <div class="notebook-resources__head">
          <span class="notebook-resources__label">Protocols cited in this record</span>
          <a class="notebook-resources__all" href="{{ basePath | default('') }}wet-lab/protocol.html">All 26 protocols &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <ul class="notebook-protocols">
          {% for id in citedProtocols %}
          <li><a href="{{ basePath | default('') }}wet-lab/protocol.html#protocol-p{{ id }}"><span class="notebook-protocols__no">{{ id }}</span><span class="notebook-protocols__title">{{ protocolTitles[id] | safe }}</span></a></li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div id="notebook-reporter" class="content-card">
      <h2>Reporter Module</h2>
      <p class="content-intro">
        This notebook records the construction and validation of our reporting system — the output module that converts PAGER receptor activation into a measurable luminescence/colorimetric signal for influenza A virus detection.
      </p>
      <div class="pdf-embed">
        <object class="pdf-embed__object" type="application/pdf"
                data="{{ basePath | default('') }}static/image/lab/wetlab/notebook/notebook-reporter-module-fix.pdf"
                aria-label="Notebook - Construction of the Reporting System">
          <p class="pdf-embed__fallback">This notebook PDF is not available yet.</p>
        </object>
      </div>
      {% set citedProtocols = ["01", "03", "04", "05", "07", "09", "10", "11", "12", "13", "14", "16", "17", "23", "24", "25"] %}
      <div class="notebook-resources">
        <div class="notebook-resources__head">
          <span class="notebook-resources__label">Protocols cited in this record</span>
          <a class="notebook-resources__all" href="{{ basePath | default('') }}wet-lab/protocol.html">All 26 protocols &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <ul class="notebook-protocols">
          {% for id in citedProtocols %}
          <li><a href="{{ basePath | default('') }}wet-lab/protocol.html#protocol-p{{ id }}"><span class="notebook-protocols__no">{{ id }}</span><span class="notebook-protocols__title">{{ protocolTitles[id] | safe }}</span></a></li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
